      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "8 Dun Oir Court is a beautifully presented semi-detached 5/6 bedroom home in Kilternan, extending to approximately 194 sqm over three floors. Generous living spaces, a flexible upper-floor layout and a landscaped west-facing rear garden combine to create an inviting home designed around family life.\n\nBuilt in 2023 and carrying an excellent A2 energy rating, No.8 offers a bright, inviting interior with a calm neutral palette and thoughtfully arranged spaces for family life. A separate ground-floor living room provides a comfortable retreat, while the kitchen and dining room opens directly to the garden, creating a natural setting for everyday meals and entertaining. The Shaker-style kitchen features quartz worktops and NEFF appliances, complemented by a separate utility room. On the first floor, a generous children`s reception room and home office offers a flexible second living space and could equally serve as a fifth bedroom. The primary bedroom occupies the front of the top floor and benefits from a walk-in wardrobe and en suite.\n\n Four bedrooms are arranged across the upper two floors, with an additional home office on the top floor. A family bathroom, an additional top-floor shower room and a ground-floor guest WC support the accommodation. The versatile first-floor reception provides the option of a fifth bedroom, allowing the layout to adapt as family needs change.\n\nThe west-facing rear garden is a standout feature of No.8. A paved terrace beside the house creates an inviting setting for outdoor dining, with a central lawn and further paving providing space to relax and entertain. Planted beds, boundary fencing and a mature tree line add greenery and a sense of privacy. A garden shed provides outdoor storage, and a side passage connects front and rear. At the front, the paved driveway offers off-street parking alongside established planting and the attractive brick facade. \n\nDun Oir Court offers a residential setting in Kilternan, within reach of the shops, cafes and everyday amenities of Stepaside and the wider Dublin 18 area. Carrickmines, Dundrum and Stillorgan provide further shopping, dining and leisure options. The location combines access to the M50 and the Luas at Leopardstown Valley with the outdoor appeal of the Dublin and Wicklow Mountains. The surrounding area offers golf, equestrian and other recreational facilities, making it an appealing base for buyers who value both suburban convenience and access to the countryside.\nThere is plenty for families to look forward to nearby, with the emerging Kilternan Village development set to bring a new village green and a welcoming centre for local life. Planned amenities include an anchor retail store, convenience shops, a cafe and restaurant, a creche, a medical centre and community facilities. Nature trails, public green spaces, play facilities and outdoor exercise areas promise more opportunities for fresh air, family outings and active afternoons. As the development progresses, these additions are set to make everyday shopping, childcare and meeting friends more convenient, further enhancing Kilternan`s appeal as a place to put down roots."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hallway - 4'9\" (1.45m) x 10'4\" (3.15m)\n1.44 m x 3.16 m. A welcoming entrance with a light-toned floor finish and neutral decor, leading into the inner hall.\n\nInner Hall - 10'0\" (3.05m) x 11'10\" (3.61m)\n3.04 m x 3.61 m. A central circulation space with a carpeted staircase, connecting the entrance hallway with the kitchen and dining room at the rear.\n\nLiving room - 12'1\" (3.68m) x 13'2\" (4.01m)\n3.68 m x 4.02 m. A bright front-facing reception room with a large window, soft neutral decoration and a timber-effect floor finish. A comfortable space for family evenings or a quieter sitting room away from the kitchen.\n\nKitchen / Dining room - 17'2\" (5.23m) x 14'6\" (4.42m)\n5.23 m x 4.41 m. An inviting kitchen and dining space with Shaker-style cabinetry, quartz worktops, NEFF appliances and a tiled splashback. There is room for a family dining table, while glazed doors connect the room to the patio and garden.\n\nUtility room - 5'4\" (1.63m) x 5'0\" (1.52m)\n1.62 m x 1.53 m. A practical utility room adjoining the kitchen, with space for stacked appliances and open shelving for everyday storage.\n\nGuest WC - 5'3\" (1.6m) x 5'0\" (1.52m)\n1.60 m x 1.53 m. A conveniently positioned guest WC with a wash-hand basin and a fresh, contemporary finish.\n\nFirst-floor landing - 7'8\" (2.34m) x 10'6\" (3.2m)\n2.34 m x 3.21 m. Carpeted landing connecting the children`s reception / home office, two bedrooms and family bathroom, with stairs continuing to the top floor.\n\nChildren`s reception / Home office / Bedroom 5 - 17'2\" (5.23m) x 13'3\" (4.04m)\n5.24 m x 4.03 m. A generous room spanning the front of the house, ideal as a combined children`s reception and home office, or as a fifth bedroom. Two windows bring in natural light, while the spacious proportions accommodate a variety of furniture arrangements. Finished with fitted carpet.\n\nBedroom 2 - 9'5\" (2.87m) x 15'8\" (4.78m)\n2.88 m x 4.78 m. A rear-facing double bedroom with fitted carpet and wardrobe storage. Soft neutral finishes create a restful bedroom setting.\n\nBedroom 3 - 7'4\" (2.24m) x 15'9\" (4.8m)\n2.24 m x 4.79 m. A second rear-facing bedroom on this level, with fitted carpet and wardrobe storage. A useful room for children, guests or a study.\n\nFamily bathroom - 5'6\" (1.68m) x 10'6\" (3.2m)\n1.68 m x 3.21 m. A contemporary tiled bathroom with bath, glazed shower screen, WC and vanity basin. A window provides natural light.\n\nSecond-floor landing - 7'9\" (2.36m) x 7'8\" (2.34m)\n2.35 m x 2.34 m. A carpeted landing serving the upper-floor accommodation.\n\nPrimary bedroom - 12'3\" (3.73m) x 16'1\" (4.9m)\n3.74 m x 4.90 m. A spacious front-facing bedroom with fitted carpet, a walk-in wardrobe and private en suite. The roofline adds character to the room.\n\nWalk-in wardrobe - 4'7\" (1.4m) x 8'4\" (2.54m)\n1.40 m x 2.55 m. A dedicated wardrobe area adjoining the primary bedroom.\n\nPrimary en suite - 5'6\" (1.68m) x 7'4\" (2.24m)\n1.67 m x 2.24 m. Private shower room adjoining the primary bedroom, with shower enclosure, vanity basin and WC.\n\nBedroom 4 - 9'5\" (2.87m) x 15'8\" (4.78m)\n2.88 m x 4.78 m. A bright rear bedroom with rooflights, fitted carpet and wardrobe storage. The sloping ceiling adds character to this comfortable room.\n\nHome office - 7'4\" (2.24m) x 13'5\" (4.09m)\n2.23 m x 4.08 m. A useful top-floor home office with a rooflight and fitted carpet, providing a dedicated space for study and working from home.\n\nShower room - 5'5\" (1.65m) x 7'9\" (2.36m)\n1.65 m x 2.35 m. An additional shower room accessed from the landing, providing a useful separate facility for the upper-floor rooms.\n\nOutside\n\nFront Garden:\nA paved driveway provides off-street parking, complemented by established planting. A side passage connects the front of the property to the rear garden.\n\nRear Garden:\nA landscaped west-facing garden with a central lawn, paved patio areas and planted boundaries, ideal for outdoor dining and relaxing in the afternoon and evening sun. A garden shed provides useful storage, with side access to the front.\n\nNotice\nThese particulars are issued by Mark Kelly & Associates (MKA) on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through us. They are provided in good faith for guidance only and do not form part of any offer or contract. MKA has not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, services or equipment, and purchasers must satisfy themselves as to their condition and working order. All descriptions, measurements, dimensions, maps, plans, photographs, condition, permissions, licences, access, prices, rents, outgoings and other information are approximate, for guidance only and may be subject to change without notice. Maps and plans are not to scale. Photographs are provided for presentation and guidance purposes. Where appropriate, AI-assisted enhancement, refinement or virtual furnishing may be used to improve presentation or assist purchasers in visualising layout, scale or potential. Such imagery is not intended to materially alter or misrepresent the structure, layout, condition or features of the property. Neither MKA nor its staff or representatives have authority to make or give any representation or warranty in relation to the property.\n"
      },
